			"date": "2025-09-10T17:49:23.606Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://sunny.garden/@knowler\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>knowler</span></a></span> oh great test cases! I noticed the same behavior in English for dictionary words and gibberish too 🤔</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115181262835042336",
			"parentId": "115181250985987400",
			"url": "https://sunny.garden/@knowler/115181262792792230",
			"author": {
				"name": "Nathan Knowler",
				"url": "https://sunny.garden/@knowler",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/286/922/977/455/165/original/45cef936319931c4.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-10T17:49:52.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> A good place to start could be making some WPTs for this, but I imagine that, like <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@famulimas\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>famulimas</span></a></span> notes, since it’s not required by the spec, it might not be accepted. I personally would expect Safari’s behaviour to be correct. I’ve ventured into some browser codebases to see if I could fix this, but I think it could be dependency related.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
