		{
			"id": "115188117701536379",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@krinkle/115188117661007679",
			"author": {
				"name": "Timo Tijhof",
				"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@krinkle",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/532/015/873/530/original/b119a0914bbd5722.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-11T22:53:09.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>A pet peeve of mine is that <a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/tags/NetNewsWire\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>NetNewsWire</span></a>, my feed reader which I otherwise love, breaks article titles rather aggressively with hyphens.</p><p>This means you get headlines like:</p><p>&gt; They Could Not Believe Al-<br>&gt; pacas Had It All.</p><p>Which is not about Artificial Intelligence-made pacas, but about Alpacas.</p><p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paca\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paca</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115192333331884739",
			"parentId": "115188117701536379",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/115192333331884739",
